    summary: 'Zero exhaust emissions, minimal mechanical moving components, instant electric motor torque profiles, and lower operating cost metrics.',
    content: 'Electric vehicles reduce your carbon footprint significantly and offer extremely quiet and smooth rides due to the absence of combustion engines. The financial advantages include low cost-per-kilometer charging, tax breaks under section 80EEB, and highly reduced routine maintenance costs.'
  },
  {
    id: 'guide-2',
    chapter: 'Chapter 02',
    title: 'Charging Explained',
    summary: 'AC Level 1/2 home setups charge overnight, while DC Fast Chargers replenish lithium modules up to 80% SoC in under 30 minutes.',
    content: 'Charging uses AC (Alternating Current) for slower home/office charging and DC (Direct Current) for high-speed highway charging stations. AC wallboxes (7.2kW to 11kW) typically charge a vehicle overnight in 6 to 10 hours. DC fast chargers (50kW to 350kW) bypass the vehicle\'s onboard charger to directly charge the battery pack, enabling rapid travel.'
  },
  {
    id: 'guide-3',
    chapter: 'Chapter 03',
    title: 'Battery Technology',
    summary: 'Modern vehicle integration uses Lithium-Iron-Phosphate (LFP) or Nickel-Manganese-Cobalt (NMC) configurations for cycle resilience.',
    content: 'Solid battery pack casing isolates cell clusters. Sophisticated liquid cooling loops regulate temperatures during rapid energy transfers. LFP batteries are highly durable and thermal-runaway resistant, whereas NMC batteries offer superior energy density for longer highway ranges.'
  },
  {
    id: 'guide-4',
    chapter: 'Chapter 04',
    title: 'Government Subsidies',
    summary: 'State subsidies and FAME-II incentives offer road tax waivers, registration exemptions, and custom income tax deductions under Section 80EEB.',
    content: 'Central FAME allocations and state incentives waive registration fees, reducing acquisition costs by up to 10-15%. Additionally, buying an EV on a loan allows tax deductions on interest paid up to ₹1.5 Lakh under section 80EEB, further reducing tax liabilities.'
  },
  {
    id: 'guide-5',
    chapter: 'Chapter 05',
    title: 'EV Maintenance',
    summary: 'No engine oil changes, spark plugs, or timing belts. Basic checks focus on coolant levels, tire wear, brake pads, and cabin air filtration blocks.',
    content: 'Maintenance schedules are highly sparse. Regenerative braking limits friction pad wear, extending mechanical component lifecycles. Routine checkups involve checking battery coolant levels, rotating tires, and replacing cabin air filters every 15,000 to 20,000 km.'
  },
